## 9d81f4236010

**Reproduced defect.** Audited generator SHA-256 `3275f9f760ac9a321bad243acd93d24752519a2f0d7450c27212ff6d635161cc`; executed canonical rule hash `631c8accd3a1`. A fresh 12-stage battery finished with 5 green and 7 failed (`checks/audit/9d81f4236010/checks/9d81f4236010_after_battery_summary.json`).

The smallest retained reproduction uses canonical labelled pair 0. The canonical Racket program accepts the input and returns the stored canonical output, but the generator's own `self_check` rejects the same input with `expected exactly one largest frame bbox`. The same source also advertises `grid_h=17` yet rejects the exact easy-band call `generate(0, 0, difficulty="easy", grid_h=17)` with `draw_int('grid_h'): override 17 outside [11, 14]`. Full input, output, apply receipt, hashes, parameters, and error strings are in `checks/audit/9d81f4236010/reproduction.json`.

The wider battery confirms this is structural rather than one bad seed:

- missing required `RULE_HASH` pin;
- canonical validator rejection across the canonical set;
- 0/60 exact canonical-profile hits, with zero support in every band;
- no semantic contract;
- at least 1,245 single-axis override findings plus 15,180 undeclared multi-axis rejections;
- active authority texts diverge exactly, although their sampled execution parity passes.

No source was edited because this was an audit-only target. Recommended repair order: synchronize/pin authority, make `self_check` own canonical lawful inputs, replace or narrow the override domains so every advertised value is constructible in every declared band, guarantee exact canonical profiles, then add executable rivals/witnesses and a lesson census.
